  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC3_Quiz_LO1_UserAccess_Q03
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: The group was given Modify rather than Full control. What does Full
    control add?
  choices:
  - The ability to open files that are in use
  - Nothing - the two are the same on a folder
  - Unlimited storage in the folder
  - The right to change the permissions and take ownership
  correctChoiceIndex: 3
  points: 10
  explanation: Modify covers reading, writing and deleting the group's own work.
    Full control lets the group rewrite the very permissions you just set, which
    defeats the point of setting them.
